PRJNA852581	SRP383489	SRR19846638	SRX15890337	SAMN29334527	GSM6266583: Col-0_W-N+_P3ID34_c; Arabidopsis thaliana; RNA-Seq	GSM6266583	GSM6266583	Arabidopsis thaliana	Multi-omics profiling of 5 Arabidopsis accessions in response to combined water and nitrogen deficiencies		W-N+	Col-0_W-N+_P3ID34_c	WT	STRESSED		leaves	leaf	Water withholding	18	Drought	Flowering stage	Col-0, Cvi-0, Shahdara, Tsu-0 and Bur-0	SWC starts to gradually differentiate between W treatments from 13 DAS, and mild drought stress is fully established after 16 DAS and then maintained constant until 31 DAS when plants are sampled.	31 DAS	Seeds—obtained altogether under controlled conditions for all genotypes and sieved to ensure homogeneous seed size within each accession—were treated with 0.1% (w/v) agarose and stratified at 4 °C in darkness for 3 d to break residual dormancy and homogenize germination. Seeds were then sown on unfertilized peatmoss soil plugs and transferred to a controlled growth chamber (8 h short day photoperiod at 230 μmol m−2 s−1 provided by 6,500 K white LED sources, with days at 21 °C/65%RH and nights at 17 °C/65%RH); after 8 d, the plugs were controlled for germination and installed on a Phenoscope robot (https://phenoscope.versailles.inrae.fr/) in the same growth chamber for 23 d under 4 different watering conditions.	31
